Feature: {featureName}
  As a {role}
  I want to {action}
  So that {benefit}

  Background:
    Given the API base URL is "{baseUrl}"
    And authentication is configured with valid credentials

  @smoke @{tag}
  Scenario: {scenarioName} - Verify successful response
    Given I have valid authentication token
    And I prepare request headers
      | Content-Type | application/json |
      | Accept       | application/json |
    When I send a {method} request to "{endpoint}"
    Then the response status code should be {statusCode}
    And the response time should be less than {timeout} milliseconds
    And the response should match the expected schema
    And the response body should contain the following fields
      | {field1} |
      | {field2} |
      | {field3} |

  @regression @{tag}
  Scenario: {scenarioName} - Verify error handling
    Given I have invalid authentication token
    When I send a {method} request to "{endpoint}"
    Then the response status code should be 401
    And the response should contain error message

  @api @{tag}
  Scenario Outline: {scenarioName} - Test with multiple data sets
    Given I prepare request with the following data
      | {key1} | <{value1}> |
      | {key2} | <{value2}> |
    When I send a <method> request to "<endpoint>"
    Then the response status code should be <statusCode>
    And the response should contain "<expectedField>"
    And the response body field "<field>" should equal "<expectedValue>"
    
    Examples:
      | {value1} | {value2} | method | endpoint | statusCode | expectedField | field | expectedValue |
      | data1    | value1   | POST   | /api/v1  | 201        | success       | id    | 123           |
      | data2    | value2   | POST   | /api/v1  | 201        | success       | id    | 124           |
      | data3    | value3   | POST   | /api/v1  | 400        | error         | msg   | Invalid       |

  @database @{tag}
  Scenario: {scenarioName} - Verify database integration
    Given I connect to the test database
    And I prepare test data in the database
    When I send a {method} request to "{endpoint}"
    Then the response status code should be {statusCode}
    And the database should contain the expected record
    And the database record should match the response data

  @performance @{tag}
  Scenario: {scenarioName} - Performance validation
    Given I prepare request for performance test
    When I send {requestCount} concurrent requests to "{endpoint}"
    Then all responses should have status code {statusCode}
    And the average response time should be less than {avgTimeout} milliseconds
    And the maximum response time should be less than {maxTimeout} milliseconds